                        "entry_id": "a2f7cf4f-a881-3bc8-b4ab-005452513f64",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Of, pertaining to, or constituting, a paragoge; added to the end of, or serving to lengthen, a word."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "eb85c4a5-79f4-4ba6-8d1c-a0711b556d28",
                                "sense_id": "b0f3ae8a-26dc-3ace-96a0-cc025b80e584",
                                "text": "In the Semitic languages, paragogic letters are added to the ordinary forms of words to express additional emphasis or a change in the meaning."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dd40295b-5f8a-4913-9e39-7dff9c20c584",
                                "sense_id": "b0f3ae8a-26dc-3ace-96a0-cc025b80e584",
                                "text": "The loss of final -n is irregular. We would rather expect *teón to develop into **θòno, with a paragogic vowel as in (Log.) sámbene' ‘blood’ < sanguen, nòmene ‘name’ < nōmen and báttoro ‘four’ < quatt(u)or."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
